      "title": "Navigation",
      "description": "Working at NTNU - NTNU Navigation Skip to Content NTNU Home Working at NTNU Search Menu Studies Master's programmes in English For exchange students PhD opportunities All programmes of study Courses Financing Language requirements Application process Academic calendar FAQ Research and innovation NTNU research Research excellence Strategic research areas Innovation resources PhD opportunities Life and housing Student in Trondheim Student in Gjøvik Student in Ålesund For researchers Life and housing About NTNU Contact us Faculties and departments Libraries International researcher support Vacancies About NTNU Maps Home Vacancies Working at NTNU Språkvelger Norsk Working at NTNU × Working at NTNU Employee benefits Application process International Researcher Support Interviews MENU Working at NTNU Working at NTNU Gløshaugen campus in Trondheim. Photo: Lars Strømman/NTNU NTNU is an attractive workplace with several campuses in Norway. About NTNU NTNU's strategy Faculties and departments Joint administration Research Innovation resources PhD opportunities Vacancies Academic posts Our work areas consist mainly of research and teaching positions in a variety of academic disciplines, ranging from junior academic roles such as research assistants and PhD candidates to associate professors («førsteamanuensis» or «dosent») and professors. Technical and administrative positions If you are seeking an academic career, NTNU offers you a wealth of opportunities. Effective administration and infrastructure are crucial for supporting core activities, including research and education. NTNU has many technical and administrative positions that ensure the university functions smoothly. We constantly need skilled employees who can provide new expertise in areas such as IT, finance, HR, and communication. NTNU in several cities NTNU has its headquarters in Trondheim, with campuses in Gjøvik and Ålesund. We also have an Oslo office (in Norwegian) for continuing education and professional development, and a Brussels office for European collaboration. Campus development at NTNU Over the next years, NTNU’s academic communities in Trondheim will be consolidated from dispersed locations into a unified campus in the area around Gløshaugen. Campus development at NTNU . Working at NTNU - video NTNU – Norwegian University of Science and Technology For employees | For students | Intranet | Canvas Studies Studies Master's programmes in English For exchange students PhD opportunities Courses Career development Continuing education Application process News News NTNU News Vacancies About NTNU About NTNU About the university Libraries NTNU's strategy Research excellence Strategic research areas Organizational chart Contact Contact Contact NTNU Employees Find experts Press contacts Researcher support Maps NTNU in three cities NTNU in three cities NTNU in Gjøvik NTNU in Trondheim NTNU in Ålesund About this website About this website Use of cookies Accessibility statement Privacy policy Editorial responsibility Facebook Instagram Linkedin Snapchat Tiktok Youtube Sign In"
